cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "DynamicsKit.jl"
abstract: >-
  A Julia library for bifurcation analysis of dynamical systems — discrete maps
  and continuous-time ODEs analysed through Poincaré sections and return maps.
  Direct exploration provides threaded parameter sweeps: 1-D diagrams, basins of
  attraction, and uniform or adaptive 2-D operating maps with period, status, and
  Lyapunov diagnostics. Continuation wraps BifurcationKit.jl pseudo-arclength with
  shooting and collocation, and extends it with codim-2 curve tracking and
  normal-form classification, connecting-orbit continuation from homoclinic to
  cycle-to-cycle connections, border-collision classification with scenario
  prediction, and grazing/sliding diagnostics for piecewise-smooth flows; an atlas
  maps periodic branches and windows automatically. An engineering layer generates
  switching maps directly from circuit descriptions, assigns branch reachability,
  computes tolerance and regime-boundary fields, certifies robust chaos over
  parameter bands and two-parameter regions, tests measured hardware routes
  against those certificates, and searches for operating points from signal
  specifications. Eligible discrete sweeps, independent-trajectory ODE maps and
  basins, and the variational continuous-flow Lyapunov field accelerate on CUDA or
  AMDGPU devices. Results serialise as versioned plain data with explicit refusal
  semantics.
type: software
